<%# One line of a transcript, wherever a transcript is read: a student's thread,
    the author's rehearsal of that same person, and the board that lays two
    rehearsals side by side.

    They were three sets of markup for one thing and had drifted into three
    different readings — the thread showing a named, timestamped paragraph at
    16px and the rehearsal showing 14px chat bubbles of the same words.

    The pending row and the settled row it is replaced by render through here
    together, which is the point. A `<p>` whose classes drift from its
    replacement moves the text at the moment the reply lands, and a bubble with
    a border and a background draws an empty box for as long as there is
    nothing in it yet. %>
<div id="<%= id %>" class="flex gap-3">
  <div class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-normal text-accent <%= from_contact ? "bg-wash" : "bg-soft" %>">
    <%= initials_for(speaker) %>
  </div>

  <div class="flex min-w-0 grow flex-col gap-2">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
      <span class="text-sm font-semibold"><%= speaker %></span>
      <%= local_assigns[:meta] %>
    </div>

    <%# body_id means "deltas stream in here", so the paragraph is drawn even
        while it is empty. Without an id, an empty body draws nothing at all —
        a contact whose whole turn was a tool call has no prose, and a bubble
        above the card carrying the actual answer reads as a failure. %>
    <% if local_assigns[:body_id].present? || body.present? %>
      <%= tag.p body, id: local_assigns[:body_id],
            class: "max-w-prose whitespace-pre-wrap break-words text-base" %>
    <% end %>

    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</div>
